{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and motion (controllable) events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery states are conservative and only allow the appropriate turn or, as a last resort, a full scan. The supervisor quickly returns to exploration after recovery, avoids oscillations, and never enables forward/random_walk in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect the robot's hardware interface.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy, enforcing safe transitions, recovery, and strong coverage bias while preventing unsafe or oscillatory actions."
  ],
  "G": [
